UID:ev_gsp_eagles_ecosystems_walk_1112-2026-11-12@coastaleventures.com
DTSTAMP:20261111T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261112T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261112T140000
SUMMARY:Eagles and Ecosystems Nature Walk at Gulf State Park
LOCATION:Gulf State Park\, Lakeview Trailhead\, 20115 State Park Road\, Gul
 f Shores\, AL 36542
DESCRIPTION:Thursday 11/12 · 1:00 PM\n\nA Gulf State Park naturalist leads
  a 1 mile walk along Eagle Loop\, on paved and boardwalk trail\, to one of
  the park's oldest bald eagle nests. The group stops at the Lake Shelby ov
 erlook and talks about how prescribed fire shapes the park's pine and mars
 h landscape. The park lists the walk as free and great for all ages\, and 
 parking at the trailhead is free.\n\nPrice: Free\n\nDetails: https://coast
 aleventures.com/events/ev-gsp-eagles-ecosystems-walk-1112.html
URL:https://coastaleventures.com/events/ev-gsp-eagles-ecosystems-walk-1112.
 html
CATEGORIES:Nature and outdoors
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
