UID:ev_fmwas_fort_pickens_bird_trip_1114-2026-11-14@coastaleventures.com
DTSTAMP:20261111T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261114T063000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261114T100000
SUMMARY:Audubon bird walk at Fort Pickens
LOCATION:Battery Langdon\, Fort Pickens\, Gulf Islands National Seashore\, 
 Battery Langdon\, Fort Pickens Rd\, Pensacola Beach\, FL 32561
DESCRIPTION:Saturday 11/14 · 6:30 AM to 10:00 AM\n\nThe Francis M. Weston 
 Audubon Society leads a guided bird walk at Battery Langdon in Fort Picken
 s. Winter birds are arriving\, so expect scaup\, bufflehead and red-breast
 ed merganser on the water and sparrows plus yellow-rumped warblers in the 
 oaks. The walk is mostly even ground with some loose sand. Registration is
  required and the walk is free\, but entering the national seashore costs 
 a park fee.\n\nPrice: Free\n\nDetails: https://coastaleventures.com/events
 /ev-fmwas-fort-pickens-bird-trip-1114.html
URL:https://coastaleventures.com/events/ev-fmwas-fort-pickens-bird-trip-111
 4.html
CATEGORIES:Nature and outdoors
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
